  "id": "COMPOUND:17163 - PROTEIN:6154",
  "verbalization": "Norarecoline is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Prelamin-A/C through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Norarecoline targets Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol and (1R,2S,6R,7R,10S,11R,12R,14S)-10,11-dihydroxy-2,6-dimethyl-12-propan-2-yl-13-oxatetracyclo[8.5.0.02,7.012,14]pentadecane-6-carboxylic acid. These compounds are all linked to Prelamin-A/C as their targets. Additionally, Norarecoline is also shown to target Teyin, which also leads to Prelamin-A/C. This suggests that Norarecoline may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving the SDR family, potentially through the inhibition of a key enzyme that is involved in the biosynthesis or regulation of Prelamin-A/C. The evidence supports a direct or indirect relationship between Norarecoline and Prelamin-A/C, likely through the SDR family of enzymes, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
